Description: Kavis boot splash — Plymouth theme and boot music
 The dark Kavis logo appears centered on a plain dark background: it
 starts at 15% opacity, becomes fully visible in about 1.5 seconds and
 gets a slight glow. Below it the product name and the italic "made by
 Karan" signature, at the bottom the "F3 — Advanced menu" and "Press
 space to skip" hints.
 .
 The boot music plays at the same time. Since Plymouth has no audio
 support, a separate systemd service manages the music; the boot splash
 does not close until the music ends. The single exception is the space
 key: when pressed the music stops and the boot continues at once. The
 behavior can be switched on and off through /etc/kavis/boot.conf. If
 there is no audio device, at most 10 seconds are waited and the boot
 continues.
 .
 The music ships embedded in the ISO, lives under /usr/share/kavis/boot/
 and is writable only by root.
